  "description": "TPO 2/1997 T1 = T184, T2 = T205, T3 = NON TPO, T4 = NON TPO, T5  = T190,\r\nT6 = NON TPO, T7 = T188, T8 = NON TPO, T9 = T186, T10 = T184\r\nT1. Holm Oak Tree. 16 metres in height. 14 metres in width. Cut back from street light by 1.5 metres, leaving the width of the tree 12.5 metres. Reduce limb that's growing towards the house by 1.5 metres. Lift to 2.5 metres as branches are low growing over footpath and road and causing a lot of fallen debris, and thin by 30% to allow more light. Tree is situated behind the rear garden of 1 Tibbets Cl, London SW19 6EF. T2. Chestnut Tree. 18 metres in height. 14 metres in width. Reduce the height by 3 metres, leaving the tree 15 metres in height. Reduce width by 2 metres all round, leaving the tree 12 metres in width, to make a more compact shape and to promote a better growth, also to cut back from the roof as tree is overgrown and now touching the building. Tree is overgrown. Situated outside the front garden of number 6/7 Tibbetts Close. T3. Purple Plum Tree. 8 metres in height. 8 metres in width. Reduce by 2 metres all round. Leaving the tree 6 metres in height and width. Tree has become overgrown and blocking sunlight. Situated outside the front garden of number 12. T4. Cherry Tree. 8 metres in height, 8 metres in width. Reduce and reshape by 1.5 metres all round 6.5 metres in height and width. Tree has become overgorwn and blocking sunlight. Remove all deadwood and remove low limb over footpath. Reducing the tree will also allow space from the tree and property as nearly touching. Situated at the front of number 16. T5. Blue Cedar Tree. 15 metres in height. 10 metres in width. Cut back from number 20 by 2 metres, leaving the tree 8 metres in width. Tree is overgrown and touching property, also blocking sunlight. T6. Pine Tree. 17 metres in height. 10 metres in width. lift low branches to 4 metre all round, as low growing over road and rear garden, causing a lot of fallen debris. Situated in the rear garden of number 21 Tilford G",
